{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id527138384"}, "name":{"label":"Ukeduke98"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2026-04-18T07:50:53-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"1"}, "im:version":{"label":"6.5"}, "id":{"label":"13971313750"}, "title":{"label":"Another subscription?"}, "content":{"label":"I know it isn’t much, but I don’t like the idea of a subscription for a weather app. Especially one that keeps trying to trick you into one. If you think that isn’t fair… read on. \n\nFeatures like “customize layout” or “change icon” are fine to be paid features. I have no issue with that. What is annoying is that the app will let you get to the setting first and then when you go to apply it it will tell you that it’s a paid feature. The UI is intentionally misleading and very frustrating as a first-time user. \n\nGray out the setting entirely and put a lock icon by it. By not doing this it makes it feel like any value is behind a paywall. I know the whole deal is that weather data isn’t free. I understand that. But then why is that the only free feature in the app? I’m fine to pay for longer forecasts or stuff like that. Or even timely weather notifications. But to add a widget? Or to change an icon? Come on. I need to pay a subscription to change an icon? How is that worth $40 a year?\n\nI am not opposed to paying for apps. I bought Dark Sky, but also appreciated that it was a one-time purchase. If this app wants to appeal to a wider audience, it needs to make some basic tweaks. I’ve heard a lot of great reviews for this app, but this experience left me severely disappointed. Not the first time I’ve tried the app either.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=961390574&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"2"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"2"}}, 
